package SyspresentDecisions {
    doc /* Product decisions and unresolved implementation choices. These records are not verification evidence. */
    comment nativeReuse /* Reuse the OpenSysML rendering contract and evaluate its canvas, layout, routing and export modules. Do not adopt the VS Code shell or demo-specific landing application. Extract a pinned browser package in David's fork if practical; otherwise use a narrowly vendored subset with license/provenance. Prototype before committing to package boundaries. */
    comment graphVersusModel /* A RenderView payload is a scoped drawing, not a complete model graph. Native-derived indexes and query results provide discovery beyond that drawing. Stable semantic identity and coverage must be explicit. */
    comment readingDesign /* Prefer scoped scenes and selective expansion. Use matrices/tables for coverage and comparisons. Preserve orientation when useful, but allow relayout to reduce crossings. Scrolling is owner preference, not a proven universal comprehension advantage. No fixed node count is claimed as a research threshold. */
    comment lifecycle /* Draft may publish as current. Current reviews may become superseded or withdrawn through the catalog. Supersession requires a replacement link; withdrawal requires a reason. The historical bundle remains unchanged. Approval is external and optional metadata does not create it. */
    comment readingControls /* Reading is the default at every viewport size. Present the narrative and a prominent model view with Fit and Explore controls. Keep contents and review metadata in disclosures; open search, filters, history and selected-element details in explicit exploration, with a single view title and a return to the authored story. */
    comment deferred /* Visual story authoring, live presenter UI, arbitrary version switching, interactive analysis/WASM execution, offline bundles, comments/accounts and automatic model diffs are outside first-release scope. Authored evolution timeline is a follow-on feature. */
    comment openDecisions /* Resolve export identity guarantees, reachable library coverage and payload size, render-kind gaps, Markdown block grammar, template accessors, package extraction feasibility, performance budgets, reader-study sample and acceptance thresholds during the initial integration spike. Do not substitute invented numerical criteria. */
}
